message.content:
{
  "generated_description": "Gross Enrolment Ratio (GER) provides education statistics on the percentage of students enrolled in primary and secondary school across different grade levels, disaggregated by gender. The indicator helps track participation in schooling and supports monitoring of access and inclusion goals. Published by NITI Aayog, the catalog focuses on GER for India, enabling comparisons over time for education planning, policy review, and program evaluation.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Elementary"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together Gross Enrolment Ratio (GER) indicators for Secondary education, highlighting differences between high and low GER States within India. It also supports international comparisons by relating India’s secondary enrolment levels to those of developing countries and selected emerging market economies. The NITI Aayog uses these education statistics to inform planning and policy discussions around access and participation in secondary schooling. The coverage is for India.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Secondary"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides Gross Enrolment Ratio (GER) indicators for secondary education (Classes IX–X) and senior secondary education (Classes XI–XII) by social groups, enabling comparisons of enrolment participation across groups. It highlights how GER changes from secondary to senior secondary levels and supports analysis of access constraints, school availability, and affordability. Published by NITI Aayog, the data is for India and is useful for education planning, equity monitoring, and policy evaluation.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Elementary"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers Gross Enrolment Ratio (GER) estimates derived from a sample survey for India, focusing on elementary education. It presents GER outcomes for the reference period 2003 to 2007, based on survey results reported for 2003 and 2007. The study was undertaken by the Programme Evaluation Organisation (PEO), Planning Commission, under the Evaluation Report on Sarva Shiksha Abhiyan, 2010, supporting assessment of enrolment trends across surveyed states and union territories. The data is useful for education planning and monitoring.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Elementary"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together Gross Enrolment Ratio (GER) indicators for Primary, Upper Primary and Elementary levels, expressed as enrolment percentages against the estimated child population for the relevant age groups. It covers the period 2001-02 to 2004-05 and supports monitoring of school participation and access across these education stages. The datasets are published under NITI Aayog and are useful for education planning, policy review, and comparative analysis of enrolment trends at primary and elementary levels in India.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Elementary"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides Gross Enrolment Ratio for Classes I–V, VI–VIII and I–VIII, covering India. It presents enrolment participation indicators for girls and boys, with state-wise breakdowns to support education planning and monitoring. The series is useful for tracking access to schooling across primary and upper primary levels and for comparing trends by gender and state. Published under the Ministry of Finance, Department of Economic Affairs, it supports evidence-based policy and economic and social development analysis.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Elementary"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together indicators on Gross Enrolment and Dropout at the primary stage (I-V) across social groups, covering SC, ST and General categories. It supports analysis of participation and retention in early schooling, enabling comparisons of enrolment levels and dropout patterns by social group. Published under NITI Aayog, the resources are focused on India and are useful for education planning, monitoring equity, and informing targeted interventions at the primary level.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Elementary"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together information on Gross Fiscal Deficit for the Eleventh Plan period, derived from the Mid-Term Review. It supports analysis of fiscal performance and deficit trends used for planning and policy assessment. The datasets are published by NITI Aayog and are focused on India, enabling comparisons across the Eleventh Plan planning cycle and review-based estimates for governance and economic monitoring.",
  "generated_sector": "Finance; Economy"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers statistics on gross generation of electricity in utilities and non-utilities, including thermal, hydro and nuclear sources. It supports analysis of electricity production trends by generation type and helps in energy planning, monitoring and reporting. Published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation, the datasets are focused on India and are useful for researchers, policymakers and analysts tracking power sector performance.",
  "generated_sector": "Power and Energy; Renewable"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Gross Irrigated Area data covers irrigation extent for multiple crops, including rice, wheat, coarse cereals, pulses, sugar-cane, spices, fruits, vegetables, and both food and non-food crops. It provides All India series from 2000-01 to 2009-10 and State-wise figures for 2008-09 and 2009-10, supporting analysis of irrigation coverage and crop-wise trends. Published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation, the catalog is useful for planning, monitoring, and evidence-based assessment of irrigation performance across India.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Irrigation"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together Gross National Product and Net National Product estimates for India across multiple years. It supports analysis of national income, economic performance, and trends in aggregate output and income measures used in policy and research. The datasets are published by the Ministry of Finance, Department of Economic Affairs, and can be used for macroeconomic reporting, comparative studies, and time-series analysis of economic indicators.",
  "generated_sector": "Finance; Economy"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together quarterly financial indicators for the telecom service sector, covering Gross Revenue (GR), Adjusted Gross Revenue (AGR), License Fee (LF), and Spectrum Charges. It supports analysis of revenue composition and regulatory charge components across telecom services, useful for policy review, compliance monitoring, and sector performance assessment. Published by NITI Aayog, the coverage is for telecom service sector data for two quarters, with geographic coverage across India.",
  "generated_sector": "Information and Communications; Telecom"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides Gross State Domestic Product (GSDP) at constant prices, capturing the volume of goods and services produced within India’s states over time, adjusted for price changes to support real growth analysis. It is useful for macroeconomic monitoring, planning, and comparative assessments of state economies using consistent monetary measures. Published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation, the datasets support research and policy work focused on domestic production and economic performance across India.",
  "generated_sector": "Economy; Macro Economy"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Gross State Domestic Product at Current Prices provides State-level estimates of the value of all goods and services produced within Karnataka during a given period, measured in monetary terms without duplication. It covers the series from 2011-12 to 2020-21, supporting analysis of economic performance using GSDP at current prices (Rs. Crore). Published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation, the data is useful for planning, policy review, and comparative economic studies over time.",
  "generated_sector": "Economy; Macro Economy"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers gross traffic earnings of Indian Railways, capturing earnings from coaching traffic (passenger and other coaching traffic), goods traffic, and other miscellaneous earnings. It supports analysis of railway revenue composition and trends in passenger and freight-related earnings for policy, planning, and performance monitoring. Published under the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation, the datasets provide India-wide coverage of railway traffic earnings.",
  "generated_sector": "Transport; Railways"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Gross Value Added by Economic Activity provides economic-activity wise estimates of gross value added for India, covering livestock-related activities at current and constant prices. Published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation through the Central Statistics Office, it supports analysis of sectoral contribution to economic growth and comparisons across time using both price bases. The catalog is useful for researchers, policymakers, and analysts tracking changes in value added by economic activity.",
  "generated_sector": "Economy; Macro Economy"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Gross enrolment ratio (GER) data provide a measure of total enrolment in a given level of education, irrespective of age, as a percentage of the eligible official school-age population for that level in a school-year. The catalog supports analysis of participation trends across education levels and can be used to assess equity-related patterns, including breakdowns by SC and ST. Published by the Ministry of Education, Department of Higher Education, it is intended for planning, monitoring, and policy evaluation for education access across India.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Elementary, Secondary"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers Gross enrolment ratio (GER) in Higher Education in India, focusing on participation in higher education for the 18-23 years age group. It presents GER as a percentage of the eligible official population, using total enrolment in higher education regardless of age. The indicators support analysis of gender-wise participation and comparisons across social categories, including SC and ST. Published by the Ministry of Education, Department of Higher Education, the data is useful for monitoring access and capacity of higher education.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Higher Education"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers gross power generation in India, detailing generation by States and Electricity Departments (EDs), along with Central sector and imports from Bhutan. It supports analysis of electricity supply composition and cross-border power inflows, useful for energy planning, performance monitoring, and policy evaluation. Published under NITI Aayog, the resources are organized to help compare gross generation contributions across administrative entities within India.",
  "generated_sector": "Power and Energy; Renewable"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers gross power generation (owned units) reported by State power utilities (SPUs) and Electricity Departments in India. It supports analysis of electricity production trends across reporting years, helping stakeholders compare utility-level performance and understand changes in generation capacity and output. Published under NITI Aayog, the collection is useful for energy planning, policy monitoring, and research on the power sector’s operational dynamics at the state utility level.",
  "generated_sector": "Power and Energy; Renewable"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers gross purchase of power (including from its owned units) by State power utilities (SPUs) and Electricity Departments (EDs) across India. It supports analysis of electricity procurement and supply-side sourcing patterns over multiple years, useful for energy planning, utility performance assessment, and policy monitoring. Published under NITI Aayog, the collection is oriented to understanding how power is acquired by state-level entities within the national electricity system.",
  "generated_sector": "Power and Energy; Renewable"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Ground Water Level Data under Atal Bhujal Yojana provides disclosed measurements of ground water levels before and after monsoon seasons. It supports monitoring and assessment of aquifer conditions across Gujarat, Haryana, Karnataka, Madhya Pradesh, Maharashtra, Rajasthan, and Uttar Pradesh. The time coverage spans 2015 to 2022, enabling trend analysis for water security planning and program evaluation under Atal Bhujal Yojana. Published by the Department of Water Resources, River Development & Ganga Rejuvenation and the Ministry of Jal Shakti.",
  "generated_sector": "Water Resources; Ground Water"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides group-wise estimates of central government civilian regular employees across India, covering ministry/department-wise and group-wise sanctioned posts and estimated positions. It focuses on labour and employment statistics for the 2009-10 to 2010-11 period, supporting workforce planning, staffing analysis, and policy monitoring. The data is published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation and is useful for comparing estimated employee strength with sanctioned positions by group and department.",
  "generated_sector": "Labour and Employment; Statistics"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides India-focused telecom market insights on GSM service subscription, covering group-wise market share in terms of subscription. It brings together service provider-wise subscriber counts (in millions) and corresponding market share, enabling comparisons across provider groups. These indicators support monitoring of competitive dynamics in the GSM segment and can be used for policy analysis, market research, and telecom planning. The data is published under NITI Aayog.",
  "generated_sector": "Information and Communications; Telecom"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together service-provider-wise statistics on subscribers in rural and urban areas, including subscriber base (in millions) and rural subscription share, alongside market share indicators. It supports analysis of telecom penetration and competitive dynamics across rural–urban segments for India. Published by NITI Aayog, the resources are useful for researchers, planners, and policymakers assessing service distribution, market structure, and inclusion trends in telecom subscriptions.",
  "generated_sector": "Information and Communications; Telecom"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides a group-wise summary of surrenderees surrendered in Manipur, supporting analysis of surrender patterns by group. It is useful for monitoring and reporting related to surrender and reintegration processes, and for policy and administrative review. The data is published by the Ministry of Home Affairs, covering Manipur as indicated in the catalog title.",
  "generated_sector": "Home Affairs and Enforcement; Enforcement Organizations"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers growing stock in forests for the top ten species, where growing stock represents the sum (by number or volume) of trees growing or living in forest areas or specified parts of forests. It supports analysis of species-wise forest biomass/stock and can be used for planning, monitoring, and policy discussions related to forest resources. Published under NITI Aayog, the scope is for India, drawing on forest inventory/reporting themes such as ISFR.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Forest Resources"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers India’s growing stock of forests and trees outside forests (TOF), using growing stock as the sum (by number or volume) of trees growing or living in forest areas or specified TOF areas. It supports analysis of forest resources and tree biomass trends for planning, monitoring, and policy use. Published under NITI Aayog, the catalog is relevant for stakeholders working with forest inventory concepts and related indicators for India.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Forest Resources"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers growing stock in Trees Outside Forest (TOF) areas for the top ten species, focusing on total volume and total stems. It supports analysis of species-wise tree resources and helps track forest-adjacent biomass and stand structure beyond designated forest lands. Published by NITI Aayog, the collection is relevant for environmental planning, biodiversity and forestry assessments, and monitoring trends using India-wide data.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Forest Resources"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers the growth of centrally funded institutions in higher education during the Eleventh Plan, tracking changes over the period 2006-07 and 2011-12. It focuses on central institutions and includes other universities/institutions such as deemed universities fully funded by the Central Government (via UGC) and institutions under other ministries. The information supports planning and monitoring of higher education capacity and institutional expansion under central funding. Published by NITI Aayog for India.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Higher Education"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers the growth of different kinds of colleges and polytechnics offering Art, Medical, Engineering and technical courses in India. It tracks changes over the period 2006-07 to 2009-10, supporting analysis of institutional expansion by course stream. The insights are useful for higher education planning, capacity assessment, and policy review. The work is published under NITI Aayog.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Higher Education"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers growth of different universities, colleges and other technical institutions in India, including Central Universities, Indian Institute of Technology, Indian Institute of Management, Indian Institute of Science, Education and Research, School of Planning and Architecture, and National Institute of Technology. It supports analysis of higher education expansion and institutional development trends across the country. Published by NITI Aayog, the collection is useful for planning, policy review, and research on education and technical education capacity.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Higher Education"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers the growth of higher education enrolment by field of study during the Eleventh Plan, comparing enrolment levels across the years 2006-07 and 2011-12. It presents figures in lakhs and percentages, supporting analysis of how different fields expanded over the plan period. Published by NITI Aayog, the collection is useful for planning, monitoring, and policy review of higher education participation trends across India.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Higher Education"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog presents growth of higher education enrolment in the Eleventh Plan by institution type and by degree/diploma type across India. It covers enrolment levels expressed in lakhs and percentage changes over the years 2006-07 and 2011-12, supporting analysis of how participation evolved by qualification and institutional category. The Ministry of NITI Aayog publishes these indicators to inform planning and monitoring of higher education expansion during the Eleventh Plan.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Higher Education"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers the growth of higher education institutions during the Eleventh Plan, focusing on degree awarding institutes, colleges, and diploma institutions. It tracks changes over the years 2006-07 and 2011-12 across central, state, and private categories. The insights support planning and monitoring of higher education capacity expansion and institutional development. Published by NITI Aayog, the coverage is for India.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Higher Education"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers growth of institutions and their enrolment during the Eleventh Plan, including degree-awarding institutions across Government, public and private providers. It supports analysis of higher education capacity expansion and student intake trends for planning and policy review. Published by NITI Aayog, the resources are focused on India and are useful for researchers, administrators and analysts assessing institutional growth and enrolment dynamics in the higher education sector.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Higher Education"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Tracks the growth of urban population in India using Census-based figures and decadal growth rates. It highlights how urban population share and absolute numbers have changed over time, including year-wise growth patterns derived from Census results. The focus is on urban demographic expansion relevant to housing demand, urban planning, and policy formulation. Published by NITI Aayog, the catalog supports analysis of trends in urbanization and their implications for urban housing and related infrastructure needs.",
  "generated_sector": "Housing; Urban Housing"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together growth projections and traffic forecasts for passenger and cargo volumes across Indian airports, expressed in MMTPA. Developed for the Twelfth Five Year Plan, it supports planning and policy use cases such as capacity assessment, infrastructure prioritization, and logistics and aviation demand analysis. The projections are published by NITI Aayog and cover airport traffic trends for India.",
  "generated_sector": "Transport; Aviation"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Growth projections for the Twelfth Five Year Plan (2012-17) provide passenger and cargo traffic forecasts for Indian airports. The forecasts present projected growth separately for passenger traffic and cargo, covering 2011 and 2017. Published by NITI Aayog, the catalog supports planning and policy analysis for airport capacity, logistics, and aviation demand management. The geographic coverage focuses on the city of passenger and cargo traffic forecasts for Indian airports named in the catalog title.",
  "generated_sector": "Transport; Aviation"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides average annual growth rates of Gross State Domestic Product (GSDP) expressed as a percentage, computed at constant prices (2004-05). It supports analysis of how state economies expand over time using a consistent price base, enabling comparisons of growth performance across India. The data is published by NITI Aayog and can be used for macroeconomic monitoring, planning, and policy evaluation focused on economic growth and price-adjusted trends.",
  "generated_sector": "Economy; Prices"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides average annual growth rates of Gross State Domestic Product (GSDP) expressed as a percentage, using current prices. It supports analysis of how state economies expand over time in nominal terms, useful for macroeconomic monitoring, planning, and policy evaluation. Published by NITI Aayog, the indicators cover GSDP growth across India, enabling comparisons of economic momentum at the state level.",
  "generated_sector": "Economy; Prices"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together information on the growth and strength of Indian shipping, focusing on the merchant shipping fleet across coastal and overseas segments. It covers key measures such as number of vessels, GRT, and the share of coastal versus overseas tonnage, supporting analysis of fleet capacity and cargo-related shipping trends. Published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation, the resources are useful for researchers and planners tracking maritime transport performance for India.",
  "generated_sector": "Transport; Water ways"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog tracks growth in MPCE(URP) at current and constant prices, based on monthly per capita consumption expenditure with a uniform reference period. It draws on four full-scale consumer expenditure surveys, including the 68th round survey, to support analysis of consumption trends over time. The Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation publishes these indicators for use in policy planning, welfare assessment, and economic research. Coverage is for India.",
  "generated_sector": "Economy; Prices"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Track the growth in wireline subscribers across India, with service-provider level indicators such as subscriber base (in millions), quarterly net additions, growth rates, and market share. The catalog supports telecom market analysis, competitive benchmarking, and monitoring of provider performance over time. Published under NITI Aayog, it is useful for researchers, analysts, and policymakers studying trends in wireline connectivity and market dynamics.",
  "generated_sector": "Information and Communications; Telecom"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers the growth of civil aviation in India, tracking key operational and economic indicators such as total fleet strength, revenues, passenger traffic (passengers carried/handled), and cargo handled. It supports analysis of how airline and airport activity evolves over time and can be used for planning, performance monitoring, and policy and investment assessments in the aviation sector. The data is published by the Ministry of Finance, Department of Economic Affairs, and focuses on India-wide trends across civil aviation operations.",
  "generated_sector": "Transport; Aviation, Finance; Economy"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog tracks the growth of higher education enrolment in Open and Distance Learning (ODL) programmes during the Eleventh Plan period. It covers enrolment changes over the years 2006-07 and 2011-12, supporting analysis of access and participation trends in distance learning. The datasets are published by NITI Aayog and are useful for planning, monitoring, and evaluating higher education expansion strategies for India.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Higher Education"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers the growth of the higher education system in India, focusing on changes in the number of universities and colleges and their enrolment. It brings together information for the years 2002 and 2007 to support trend analysis of institutional expansion and student participation. The insights are useful for planning, monitoring, and policy discussions around higher education capacity and access. The catalog is published by NITI Aayog.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Higher Education"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers the growth of Indian shipping, tracking coastal and overseas shipping activity through measures such as number of vessels and GRT, along with the share of coastal and overseas in Indian tonnage. It presents age-wise details as on 31st December, supporting analysis of fleet composition and trends over time. Published by the Ministry of Ports, Shipping and Waterways, the resources are useful for planning, monitoring maritime capacity, and understanding shifts between coastal and overseas segments across India.",
  "generated_sector": "Transport; Water ways"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers growth of output, inputs and productivity in the agriculture sector, focusing on value of output, value of intermediate inputs, and gross value added at 2004-05 prices. It also tracks factor inputs and partial factor productivities across major agricultural policy and planning phases, including the Pre-Green Revolution period, Green Revolution period, Wider Coverage period, Early Liberalization period, Ninth Plan period, Tenth Plan period and Eleventh plan period. Published by NITI Aayog for analysis of agricultural performance and productivity trends across India.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Crops"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together statistics on the growth of Postal Life Insurance (PLI) and Rural Postal Life Insurance (RPLI) in India. It covers key performance indicators such as policy achievements, sum assured, and premium income, supporting analysis of insurance outreach and rural coverage trends. The datasets are useful for monitoring sector performance, assessing growth over time, and informing policy and planning. Published under the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation.",
  "generated_sector": "Finance; Insurance"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides an at-a-glance view of telecom service growth in India, covering wireline and wireless subscribers (in million) across urban and rural areas. It also tracks key performance indicators such as teledensity (wireline, wireless, rural and urban), telecom traffic measured in MOU for GSM and CDMA, and ARPU (Rs. per subscriber per month) for GSM and CDMA. These indicators support monitoring of connectivity expansion and service usage trends for planning and policy analysis by NITI Aayog.",
  "generated_sector": "Information and Communications; Telecom"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers the growth pattern of livestock population in India, focusing on species-wise livestock population and compound annual growth rates (%). It supports analysis of trends in livestock numbers over time for planning, monitoring, and policy formulation in animal husbandry and related development. The datasets are published by the Department of Animal Husbandry and Dairying and the Ministry of Fisheries, Animal Husbandry and Dairying, enabling researchers and administrators to compare growth dynamics across livestock species.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Animal Husbandry"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog focuses on gymnasium-related transactions in Ahmedabad, Gujarat, covering counts of transactions and the associated amounts. It supports monitoring and analysis of gymnasium usage and financial activity within the city, useful for urban service planning and performance tracking under the Smart Cities Mission. Published by the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs with Smart Cities Mission partners including Gujarat and Ahmedabad, the coverage is city-specific for the Gymnasium initiative in Ahmedabad.",
  "generated_sector": "Urban; Development"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides an overview of Habitation coverage under Bharat Nirman, tracking progress in extending road connectivity to habitations. It supports monitoring and evaluation of infrastructure coverage initiatives and helps stakeholders assess performance over time. Published by NITI Aayog, the resources focus on road transport coverage across India, enabling comparisons and planning for further connectivity improvements.",
  "generated_sector": "Transport; Road Transport"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers hawkers licence issuance for the City of Ahmedabad, Gujarat, supporting access to licensing-related information for street vendors. It brings together records and details on how hawkers licences are issued under the Smart Cities Mission framework, enabling stakeholders to understand licensing coverage and administrative processes. Useful for municipal planning, compliance and governance, and research on urban street vending regulation in Ahmedabad.",
  "generated_sector": "Urban; Development"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together information on hazardous waste contaminated dump sites, focusing on their state-wise distribution and the number of such sites identified through monitoring by the Supreme Court Monitoring Committee (SCMC). It compiles reporting linked to the Ministry and related pollution control processes involving CPCB and court oversight. The datasets support environmental compliance review, risk assessment, and policy planning for hazardous waste management across India.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Hazardous Waste"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog focuses on the requirement of a head master for Ujjain, covering the City of Ujjain, Madhya Pradesh. It consolidates information related to the “Head Master Required” notice for use in local administrative follow-up and recruitment-related workflows. Published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs within the Smart Cities Mission framework, it supports stakeholders seeking head master appointment details for the specified city.",
  "generated_sector": "Governance and Administration; Union/State Government Administration"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together estimates of the headcount ratio and the number of poor persons (in lakh) for India, covering both rural and urban areas. It spans 1973-74, 1983, 1993-94 and 2004-05, enabling comparisons of poverty levels across time and settlement type. The indicators support policy analysis and monitoring of poverty reduction efforts by NITI Aayog, including planning and evaluation of targeted interventions.",
  "generated_sector": "Social Development; Women"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together indicators on poverty in India, focusing on the headcount ratio and the number of poor persons below the poverty line for both rural and urban areas. It supports analysis of how poverty levels vary across settlement types and over time, enabling comparisons for policy planning and monitoring. Published under NITI Aayog, the resources are useful for researchers, analysts, and decision-makers working on development and poverty reduction strategies.",
  "generated_sector": "Social Development; Women"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers health information for Diu, focusing on incidences and patients of water borne and vector borne diseases within the Diu municipal council. It supports monitoring of disease patterns linked to water and vectors, and can be used for public health planning, targeted interventions, and urban health reporting under the Smart Cities Mission. The datasets are published by the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs, Daman and Diu, Diu, and relate specifically to the City of Diu, Daman and Diu.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides ward-wise health infrastructure details for Indore, Madhya Pradesh, covering public and private facilities across primary, secondary and tertiary levels. It compiles facility names and types along with key capacity and staffing indicators such as number of beds, doctors, physicians, nurses and midwives. The information supports planning and monitoring of urban health services at the ward level, including maternity-related service availability. It is published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs through the Smart Cities Mission for Indore.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog focuses on health and healthcare services for Kohima, Nagaland, covering key urban service elements such as ambulance availability and hospitals/dispensaries. It is intended to support monitoring and planning of city-level health service delivery under the Smart Cities Mission. Published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs with participating agencies in Nagaland and Kohima, the resources help stakeholders assess access to essential care and emergency response services within the city.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Health-focused data for New Town Kolkata, West Bengal, under the Smart Cities Mission. The catalog supports sharing of urban health indicators and related information such as hospital and vaccination data, including COVID-related themes. It is intended to help planners, researchers, and local stakeholders monitor public health needs and track service delivery in the city. Published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs with participation from Smart Cities Mission and the concerned state and city entities.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together health-related information for Pimpri Chinchwad, Maharashtra, focusing on women, children, and water-borne diseases. It supports analysis of key disease themes such as child and water conditions and women’s health needs, enabling targeted planning and monitoring for urban health interventions. Published under the Smart Cities Mission and the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs, the resources are intended for city-level stakeholders working on improved health outcomes.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog focuses on health-related information for Satna, covering health infrastructure and related indicators relevant to urban service delivery. It supports planning and monitoring of local health infrastructure under the Smart Cities Mission, with inputs associated with the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs and the Madhya Pradesh and Satna administrations. The scope is limited to the City of Satna, Madhya Pradesh, enabling city-level use cases such as benchmarking, gap analysis, and evidence-based improvements to health services.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together information on health care facilities in Pune, Maharashtra, supporting planning and service delivery for urban health needs. It focuses on the availability and coverage of health facilities within the city, helping residents, administrators, and program managers locate relevant services and identify gaps. Published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs through the Smart Cities Mission, the resources are intended to strengthen city-level health infrastructure and accessibility.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together information on health care facilities in Tiruppur, Tamil Nadu, covering both public and private providers. It focuses on key service points such as dispensaries and primary hospitals, along with government and public hospitals. Designed to support local planning and easier discovery of health infrastructure, the resources align with the Smart Cities Mission under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs. The coverage is city-level for the City of Tiruppur, Tamil Nadu.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
